      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 307: 🔴 RTCP demux relies on `RTP_PT_IS_RTCP(buf[1])` alone, which can misclassify valid RTP packets when marker bit is set (e.g., RTP PT 72–95 produces second-byte values overlapping RTCP types). In rtcp-mux mode this can route RTP into the RTCP path and break media/interoperability. Implement RFC5761-compliant demux (at minimum: RTCP type range 200–211 with robust validation) and/or enforce negotiated RTP payload types to avoid the collision range.",
      "revId": "a92aa3cd24448f7d5bd03b05199045986ecc042e",
